{
  "_comment": "Measurements of the AI-generated interiors (Nano Banana, Nov 2026), in pixels of the file in mockups/scenes/. scripts/calibrate-rooms.py turns each into a calibrated scene in scenes.json. Straight-on rooms: wall = [left, top, right, bottom] of the back wall, heightCm = the real height between top and bottom (from the prompt's ceiling height, checked against furniture). clear = [x from, x to] of open wall; furnitureTop = highest pixel of anything in front of that wall (sofa back, headboard, lamp, plant); topLimit = lowest pixel of anything hanging from the ceiling. Angled rooms give the full quad and a focal length instead. centreX = the pixel column to centre works on (the sofa, bed or desk below). hangAbove = hang a set gap above the furniture rather than at eye level. Angled rooms give quad, widthCm, heightCm, focalPx and principalY (the horizon: these images are shot as if with a shift lens).",
